Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: hand off overlapping background CAC before new CAC state

Adapt MediaTek SDK 25.12 patch0026, StanleyYP Wang, pinned 08196fa6.
Backports 7.2 tracks background CAC with background_radar_wdev instead of
the old boolean. Place the abort after a successful foreground driver call
but BEFORE cfg80211_set_cac_state(true): abort itself clears shared channel
CAC state in this API. Preserve background ownership on driver errors.
No default radar enablement, channel selection, or regulatory changes.

--- a/net/wireless/nl80211.c
+++ b/net/wireless/nl80211.c
@@ -11957,6 +11957,19 @@
 					 link_id);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
+
+	/* A background CAC on an overlapping channel must not complete after
+	 * foreground CAC starts. In this API its wdev records active ownership;
+	 * there is no background_cac_started flag. Abort before publishing the
+	 * new CAC state, since abort clears the overlapping channel's state.
+	 * A failed foreground start must retain the previous background CAC.
+	 */
+	if (rdev->background_radar_wdev &&
+	    rdev->background_radar_chandef.chan &&
+	    cfg80211_is_sub_chan(&chandef,
+				rdev->background_radar_chandef.chan, false))
+		cfg80211_stop_background_radar_detection(
+			rdev->background_radar_wdev);
 
 	switch (wdev->iftype) {
 	case NL80211_IFTYPE_AP:
